          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Origins of the Conflict</strong><br>\nThe Middle East conflict has its roots in various historical and political developments. A central cause lies in the territorial claims based on historical and religious ties. Particularly, the area around Israel and Palestine is at the center of the conflict, as both peoples lay claim to the same territory.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Zionism and Arab Nationalism</strong><br>\nTwo important movements that have shaped the conflict are Zionism and Arab Nationalism. Zionism aimed for a Jewish state in historical Palestine, while Arab Nationalism sought the independence and unity of the Arab peoples. These opposing ideologies led to tensions and conflicts in the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>UN Partition Plan of 1947</strong><br>\nThe UN Partition Plan of 1947 was an attempt to find a solution to the Jewish-Arab conflict. The plan proposed dividing Palestine into a Jewish and an Arab state. However, the plan was rejected by the Arab side, leading to further confrontations.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
