            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Six-Day War 1967</strong><br>\nThe Six-Day War in 1967 was a significant turning point in the Middle East conflict. Israel was able to capture large areas, including the Sinai Peninsula, the Gaza Strip, the West Bank, and the Golan Heights. The occupation of these territories led to ongoing tensions and conflicts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Settlement Construction and Occupation</strong><br>\nA key issue in the Middle East conflict is Israeli settlement construction in the occupied territories. The international community considers this settlement construction to be illegal. The occupation and settlement construction have led to significant tensions between Israelis and Palestinians.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Terrorism and Violence</strong><br>\nTerrorism and violence are tragic manifestations of the Middle East conflict. Attacks and military confrontations have cost countless lives and further poisoned the relationship between the conflicting parties. Both sides have used violence over the years to achieve their goals.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
