          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Peace Processes</strong><br>\nThere have been various attempts to resolve the Middle East conflict through negotiations. Peace processes like the Oslo Accords or the Roadmap for Peace were meant to pave the way for a two-state solution. However, to date, these efforts have not led to a lasting solution.</p>\n\n<p><strong>International Involvement</strong><br>\nThe international community, including the USA and other major powers, has intervened in the Middle East conflict over the years. This involvement has often influenced the dynamics of the conflict and complicated the relations between the conflicting parties.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Humanitarian Crises</strong><br>\nThe ongoing conflicts have led to serious humanitarian crises. Living conditions in the occupied territories are often very difficult, and the civilian population suffers from poverty, unemployment, and a lack of basic infrastructure. The humanitarian situation is another urgent issue in the context of the Middle East conflict.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
